# Build output and caches. .zig-cache alone is ~488 MB and rebuilds on
# demand; zig-out is the produced binary.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/

# B2's runtime stubs (tests/b2_runtimes.ps1) -- build output, not vendored
# source: 5 platforms, ~6 s to regenerate. Whether these ship the way bin/
# does is a B3 question, once `ringpp build` is the thing consuming them.
# Matches only the platform subdirectories -- runtime/README.md, sitting
# directly in runtime/, is untouched by this pattern and stays tracked.
runtime/*/

# Scratch data written by examples. Example 05 builds a data file and
# removes it, but a run killed mid-way leaves one behind.
_example*.bin
_p05*.bin
_probe*.bin

# Ring/Softanza engine artefacts
*.ringo
*.obj
*.pdb

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~

# Ring++ is dependency-free. `.central/` is coordination state from
# the Softanza estate's harness -- an inbox, an outbox and a status page --
# which was tracked here and does not belong in a public Ring package.
# Ignored rather than merely deleted: the harness may write it again, and a
# regenerated file must not silently re-enter the history.
.central/

# Same reason: Central rewrites WHATS-NEXT.md with the estate's cross-repo
# plan (reference-design versions, the UI law, contracts) and instructions to
# open a mailbox under D:/GitHub/softanza. None of that is Ring++'s roadmap
# or a reader's business. Ring++'s own plan is docs/PHASE_PLAN.md.
WHATS-NEXT.md

# Android demo: the build directory `ringpp build --target android` writes,
# which holds the generated manifest, Java, dex and the debug signing key.
# A signing key never belongs in a repository, even a throwaway one.
#
# `android/report.txt` was ignored here until 2026-08-26. It was not a build
# artefact -- it was the demo program's own output, proof that `ring -go` was
# executing the program while packaging it (FINDINGS F-37). Ignoring it made
# the symptom invisible for as long as the entry existed. The entry is gone,
# and so is the behaviour that produced the file.
android/out/
android/app.ringo
